                <pb facs="0820" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg700"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.48/3827: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mexico City</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Frazer</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-15T13:00:00-07:00">January 15, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Earthquake occurred last evening wide area central and southern Mexico. One
                    person reported killed and 25 injured and over 50 buildings seriously damaged
                    this city. Believe no American citizens or American interest suffered.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frazer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
